<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
    HSK patch: hide VFEA_ElectricMendingStation and VFEA_FueledMendingStation
    from the architect/build menu.

    Why?
    Core_SK already provides a HSK-tuned mending workbench
    (HSK's MendingBench / MendingTable). Having the VFE Ancients mending
    stations show up in the architect menu would give players two parallel
    mending systems with overlapping recipes — confusing and redundant.

    What's preserved:
    - The ThingDef itself still exists (so it can spawn pre-built inside
      VFE Ancients vault layouts, where the player encounters it as
      ancient-tech loot they can salvage or use in-place)
    - The associated RecipeDef (Recipes_Mending.xml) and WorkGiverDef
      remain functional, so any vault-spawned mending station still works
    - The research prerequisite (VFEA_Mending) still loads, in case
      something else references it

    What's hidden:
    - Player cannot construct a new VFEA mending station from the
      Production architect tab. Use HSK's Mending Workbench instead.

    Implemented as PatchOperationRemove on <designationCategory> rather
    than removing the whole def — preserves existing vault content but
    cleans up the architect menu.
-->
<Patch>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
        <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEA_ElectricMendingStation"]/designationCategory</xpath>
    </Operation>

    <Operation Class="PatchOperationRemove">
        <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="VFEA_FueledMendingStation"]/designationCategory</xpath>
    </Operation>

</Patch>
